WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.840
The trailer opens with this metronome, the
same device that psychic medium Elise Rainier

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.500
used to hypnotize Josh Lambert in the first
Insidious so that he could go into the Further

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.590
and rescue his son.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.360
The reappearance of it here suggests that
he’ll be going back into The Further to

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.849
settle some unfinished business.

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:16.520
There’s also a shot of someone using a digital
metronome propped up on the side of a bed.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.109
Dalton used to astral project in his sleep
before being hypnotized to forget about his

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:22.370
ability at the end of Insidious Chapter 2.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.650
I cringe for this USB port, but I would guess
that this is Dalton, trying to rediscover

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.010
the mysteries of his past.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:32.540
We’re shown flashes of the family’s past
in Insidious 1 and 2, before being taken forward

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.989
10 years, with Dalton set to head off to college.

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:39.690
To learn whose funeral the family is attending,
what happened to Josh over the years and what

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.217
might be hidden in each Insidious logo, stick
around to the end of this video.

00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.567
♪ (metal intro) ♪

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.250
Welcome to Things You Missed, trailer edition.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.230
Today I’m looking at the first trailer for
Insidious: The Red Door.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.340
Since the trailer glosses through things pretty
quickly, I thought it would be a good idea

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.870
to go back through shot by shot and analyze
what we’re supposed to take away from the

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:02.870
trailer.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.560
Insidious: The Red Door is the long awaited
follow up to the Lambert family story.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.630
The last two movies were prequels, exploring
the past of Elise.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.480
So we never got to see what happens after
ghost Elise discovered The Red Face demon

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.860
haunting a new family.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.340
But we are definitely going to.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.095
Let’s cut in to the Things You Missed.

00:01:17.095 --> 00:01:21.715
♪ (ominous music) ♪

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.439
At the end of the second movie, Josh and Dalton
are hypnotized to erase their abilities to

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:29.560
astral project into The Further because of
the danger associated with it.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.619
I’ve been saying for like 10 years now that
this was not a good idea, because Josh forgot

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:37.740
his ability when he was a kid, and this left
him very ill prepared when his son demonstrated

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.119
the ability years later.

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:41.920
They would have been better off learning to
harness their abilities like Elise.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.780
Sure enough, another 10 years go by, meaning
that The Red Door is set in 2020.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.630
It seems like a lot of movies just like to
exist in a universe where COVID never happened

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.630
for some reason.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.130
It’s weird, because I can’t really think
of any movies set in 1940s Germany that don’t

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.259
acknowledge the Holocaust.

00:01:56.259 --> 00:01:59.789
Maybe the pain from COVID is still too fresh
for screenwriters to want to think about it.

00:01:59.789 --> 00:02:03.570
Josh is seen doing a memory exercise where
he flips over photos of his family members.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:07.490
He seems to be in a new house, and it’s
good to see that they got a new armchair rather

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.530
than keeping that one that Elise died on.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.920
It seems he’s beginning to see ghosts again,
and his nightmares have come back.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.019
As a kid, he would astral project in his sleep,
which he perceived as a series of nightmares.

00:02:17.019 --> 00:02:20.350
The shot where he wakes up is deliberately
framed so we don’t see the other side of

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.490
his bed, and in all the shots where he’s
at home, he’s alone, leading me to believe

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.990
that he and Renai may not be together anymore.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.660
Add that to the fact that he’s got all these
photos of her around the house… it makes

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.950
it look like he misses her.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.170
Renai also suggests he drive Dalton to college
to reconnect, which may suggest that they’ve

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.170
been apart.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.830
When driving Dalton to college, he’s holding
something, possibly some kind of cigar, which

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.890
could also be a clue about his issues.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.210
Maybe I’m totally over speculating, but
it’s possible that his memory issues are

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.590
connected to relationship issues with his
family.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.760
The only time he and Renai are seen together
is at this funeral.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.810
And speaking of which, who died?

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:57.540
The kids are grown up in this shot, so this
isn’t Elise’s funeral, it’s 10 years

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.540
later.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.540
There are four characters who don’t appear
in the trailer: The paranormal investigators

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.257
Specs and Tucker, Elise’s ghost hunter colleague
Carl, and Josh’s mom: Lorraine.

00:03:06.257 --> 00:03:09.010
I’m going to guess that they’re attending
Lorraine’s funeral, since they’re probably

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.690
not still in contact with Specs, Tucker and
Carl, especially if they potentially don’t

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.790
remember much of what took place in 2010.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.290
Her death would be significant, because assuming
Josh and Dalton lost their memories, that

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.319
would leave Renai as the only one who truly
remembers everything that went on in 2010,

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:25.280
and she’ll be dealing with the difficult
quandary of whether or not to remind them

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.519
of those painful memories.

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:27.840
– [Renai] There’s so much you don’t know.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.819
And I was too scared to tell you the truth.

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:32.330
– OK, so Dalton is going to college for art
school.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.790
– You’re old now.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.140
– No Dalton, you’re old now!

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.180
Interestingly in the trailer, he says he was
in a coma when he was 10.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.439
In the script of Insidious, it suggests that
he was 8, but as we know the ages used in

00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:44.640
scripts are not canon.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.159
He looks more like he was 8 in the original,
and it would make sense if he was going to

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:50.239
college for the first time at 18.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:53.890
But it could also make sense that he was 10, and
he started at a local community college for

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.640
the first two years, and now, 10 years later,
he’s 20 years old and transferring away

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.549
to university to study art.

00:03:59.549 --> 00:04:02.890
Josh has some kind of artwork in his house
next to his pictures of Renai, which I’m

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:04.950
guessing is something that Dalton drew at
some point.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.370
It’s fitting that he would become an artist,
because he loved to draw as a kid, in fact,

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:11.629
his drawings of what he saw in the Further
are what caused his parents to realize his

00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:13.599
ability to astral project was real.

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:16.611
His art teacher talks about balancing light
and dark in his compositions.

00:04:16.657 --> 00:04:20.040
And there’s a double meaning here, because
light and dark are terms sometimes used in

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.410
this franchise to describe the real world,
the light, and The Further, the dark.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.740
And we see the beginnings of him drawing the
red door.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.410
This suggests that it’s happening again.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:32.150
Some of the pictures he drew as a kid were
pictures of the red doors that connect certain

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.280
areas in The Further.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.090
The art teacher tells him to…

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:40.910
– sink deep into your memory and let’s
see what light can find.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.500
– So I would surmise that his investigation
into this missing area of his memory causes

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.690
his astral projection ability to resurface
and cause The Red Face demon to have another

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:52.880
opportunity to possess Dalton’s body, just
as he had 10 years before.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.960
In one shot we see Red Face reach out and
grab Dalton’s hand, leaving a big gash with

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.540
no blood, very similar to the injury that
Elise sustained in the 1980s when investigating

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.470
Josh’s paranormal issues with The Bride in
Black.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.320
Speaking of whom, when I first saw the trailer,
I was confused because these are new photos

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.630
that we haven’t seen before.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:13.060
We know The Bride in Black appears in the
background of photos taken of his target.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.199
However, I believe these are just supposed
to be old photos of Josh that just weren’t

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:17.479
shown in the previous movies.

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:21.130
In Insidious 1, the photos are used to explain
to him what happened in his childhood, so

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.070
that’s probably what’s going on here again.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.570
I don’t think The Bride is back.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.480
It would be pretty disappointing if he came
back, because if that were the case, then

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.229
what was the point of the 2nd movie?

00:05:29.229 --> 00:05:32.630
I do think that there are going to be new
photographs that feature a different lurking

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:33.630
entity however.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.020
Dalton meets a girl at college and we see
them take a selfie together, but the trailer

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.800
doesn’t show the result of the photo.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.789
However, we do see familiar things start to
happen, like a red handprint appearing on

00:05:42.789 --> 00:05:43.339
Dalton’s bed.

00:05:43.339 --> 00:05:47.090
While Dalton was in a coma in 2010, the family
discovered something similar on his bedsheet

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.900
before all hell broke loose.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.360
We also see Red Face putting on his favorite
record by Tiny Tim, and what appears to be

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:55.889
Josh and Dalton approaching the red door and
entering Red Face’s lair.

00:05:55.889 --> 00:05:59.169
In Insidious, as the ghosts around the house
started to smell Dalton’s empty vessel,

00:05:59.169 --> 00:06:02.510
they got closer and started appearing more
frequently in the real world.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.400
One of them sticks a hand out of a drawer
as Specs is closing it.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.930
In the new trailer, we see something similar,
a hand protruding out of a wall.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.780
Like the other films, there will probably
be an array of ghosts outside of the main

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.400
threat, some good, some neutral, some evil.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.810
In this shot, Dalton discovers someone wrapped
in plastic, and if we bring up the lights,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.870
there’s another creepy looking figure in
the distance.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.699
There’s also a shot of someone aiming a
flashlight towards the demon, and you can

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.520
see another entity moving around in the background.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.520
Watch your back.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.680
We also see a new entity crawling out from
under a bed.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.680
It looks kind of like this creature, who was
shot for Insidious The Last Key, but ultimately

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.020
never featured in the movie.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.580
Closer to the end of the trailer, Dalton gets
dragged away with a chain on his foot, the

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.419
same way he was confined by Red Face in Insidious
1.

00:06:39.419 --> 00:06:44.350
Additionally, there’s this part, where the
adult Dalton, Adulton if you will, sees the

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:47.949
scene from the end of Insidious Chapter 2
of his Dad, who is possessed at the time,

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:49.990
nearly about to strike him down with the hammer.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:53.630
Remember, one of the traits of The Further
is it is not tied to time in the same way

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:54.630
that our world is.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.539
It can show you different events from different
points in time.

00:06:57.539 --> 00:07:01.050
Since Dalton doesn’t remember the events
of Insidious Chapter 2, he probably thinks

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.050
this is real.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:05.819
We also see one of his paintings is a man
with a hammer standing in front of a red door,

00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:08.550
maybe a result of his foggy memories of the
2nd film.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:10.600
We also see a return of the can phone.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:14.190
In Insidious 2, this was how Dalton and Foster
communicated when they were supposed to be

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:17.540
in bed, but it was later compromised by the
ghosts in the Further, trying to communicate

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.540
with Dalton.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.830
He also used it to his advantage at the end,
as a way to find his way out of the Further

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.080
after locating his dad.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.110
As for Elise, it seems she’s getting the
old Randy Meeks treatment this time around.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.360
After her death in the first Insidious, she
helped out as a ghost in Insidious Chapter

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.060
2, claiming that she moved on to see a better
place, which is implied to be the equivalent

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:38.180
of heaven, but came back when she realized
the Lambert family was still in trouble.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:44.520
– I’ve seen that better place, but I came
back here because I heard you calling and I think I can help.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.150
– Chapter 2 ends with her as a ghost, joining
Specs and Tucker on their investigations,

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.720
although it appears that only little kids
can see her.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.380
But after 10 years, you have to figure she
would have moved on to that better place,

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:57.130
permanently, because there is no joy in staying
in The Further.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:08:00.050
Plus, she would probably want to be on and
be with her husband again.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:04.100
It’s not clear if a ghost can come back
to the Further after entering the better place

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.160
beyond the Further.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.330
At the end of the trailer we see the Insidious:
The Red Door logo.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:11.340
This is actually something I’ve been waiting
for too, because I’ve spent probably too much

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.650
time thinking about the Insidious logos.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:17.750
Starting with the second movie, the letters
SI are colored red, and I was always curious

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.350
if there was some meaning there.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.080
In the third one the three I’s are red,
which seems to make sense.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.990
It’s the third chapter and three Is represent
the roman numeral three.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:31.889
Then The Last Key logo actually looks different in the trailer than it does on the poster, which made me question if there is any pattern to this

00:08:31.889 --> 00:08:32.889
at all.

00:08:32.889 --> 00:08:36.570
So the new logo has the SI colored red once
again, which I think may be an intentional

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.219
call back to the second film.

00:08:38.219 --> 00:08:41.419
This is the true follow up to the Lambert
family story that we’ve been waiting for,

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:43.479
so it’s logo will follow that of the second
movie.

00:08:43.479 --> 00:08:46.980
If that’s the case, it’s a lot simpler
than I thought it was going to be, for a while

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.171
I thought there was going to be some secret
message there, but I think that’s all it is.

00:08:50.171 --> 00:08:53.540
But before the new Insidious comes out this
July, you need to get fully caught up on your

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.100
Insidious lore, so check out that playlist
on the left.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:59.352
I’ve got a ton of Insidious content planned
before then, so make sure you don’t miss

00:08:59.352 --> 00:09:03.790
out on that by subscribing to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ringing the deathbell

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.067
for all notifications and I’ll see you in
the next one.

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:09.000
Assuming we both survive.

